{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1539579-initiative","id":1539579,"title":"Initiative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-31T01:14:30-07:00","id":1539579,"title":"Initiative","content":"I'm curious to know what other people think about the Initiative system in Curseborne/Storypath Ultra. Personally I absolutely hate it. All you need is one character with a super high initiative and the rest can use it as a dump stat, because all you need is one character to go first and they all will. You don't have to worry if your character is slow or has a bad reaction time, because as long as one character goes first, suddenly all the characters have super speed. You might as well just have it as a group roll, one roll for all the characters, one roll for all the badguys, the side that rolls highest wins. Or why even have a roll at all, just let the players pick and choose who goes when. Of course that makes absolutely no sense because in combat there's no way you can pick and choose who goes when. People who are slower or have worse reactions will almost always go after people who are faster or have better reaction times. The initiative system doesn't make any sense mechanically or logically. I'm definitely going to ditch the initiative system and just have everyone go in order of most hits on the initiative roll to lowest. I honestly don't know why the system doesn't already do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T02:00:13-07:00","id":1539581,"title":"","content":"I agree with you. I prefer each one with their own initiative as it opens space for strategy related to the actions being taken, like preparing against an attack or to prepare to act just before another character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T03:08:05-07:00","id":1539582,"title":"","content":"I generally also goes for classical <i>'Each roll their own Initiative'</i>, not this <i>'<b>Popcorn Initiative</b> players choose who goes after each'</i>. It's greater trend in RPG products, not only from Onyx Path. Onyx is going with 'Popcorn Initiative' in <b>Realms of Pugmire 2E</b> - I also plan to hack it for more classical 'Turn Order' Initative. Just use normal 'we roll separately each' and go with that. VTT even likes more this classical take as it's easier to program for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm really starting to wonder if this whole '<b>Popcorn Initiative</b> trend' in RPGs is not to different from D&amp;D much more? \ud83e\udd14 In <b>Realms of Pugmire</b> it can be, as they want <b>Onyx20</b> mechanics to be legally different from normal <b>d20 </b>engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2024, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T06:19:20-07:00","id":1539584,"title":"","content":"OPP has been using popcorn initiative way before the D&amp;D issues. It goes back at least to the first edition of Pugmire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T06:41:06-07:00","id":1539586,"title":"","content":"Its pretty easy to use the old initiative that Storypath games used if you need to. For me, I like popcorn initiative because it allows me to keep the players more engaged at the table. Often times with traditional initiative you'll get a player who doesn't get to do as much as the other players and with popcorn I feel like it can allow me as a GM to toss it to them if after my turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}